{
  "_contract": {
    "name": "managed captcha evidence, layout-filtered",
    "purpose": [
      "ONE FILE, TWO REPOS, BYTE IDENTICAL. student-outreach-backend emits the action list and consumes",
      "the result; stratus-browser-cloud executes the actions and produces the result. Neither repo can",
      "import the other, so the contract between them used to be a hand-written literal in each, which",
      "is exactly how pass.scope.scopeKind diverged and blocked every submission in this product for a",
      "day.",
      "This file is the shared artifact instead. `actions` is what the backend really builds; `emitted`",
      "is what the runner really returned for `html`; `expected` is what the backend's predicates really",
      "conclude. The stratus test serves `html`, runs `actions` through the shipped runner and asserts",
      "the emission matches. The backend test asserts its builder still produces `actions` and its",
      "predicates still produce `expected` from `emitted`. Either side drifting fails its own suite in",
      "its own repo, with the same file naming the disagreement.",
      "Regenerate by running the stratus test with CAPTCHA_CONTRACT_WRITE=1, then copy the file into the",
      "backend unchanged."
    ],
    "measured": "2026-08-12, read-only sweep of 30 live postings in real Chromium",
    "backendBase": "aed9b5d026159e42a58eb5a4cca58d76e379af44",
    "stratusBase": "47488714a682ab3938d38d713059a55639f76903",
    "fixtureHosts": [
      "Iframe srcs keep the production path and query and drop the scheme and host, so the fixture is",
      "offline and deterministic. Every predicate on both sides reads the path and query only; the host",
      "appears in none of them."
    ]
  },
